Q: problems with siteMap in Web.config A: <p>The <code>web.sitemap</code> file is the default site-map provider for ASP.NET, so it will work without specifying the <code>&lt;siteMap ...</code> in <code>web.config</code>. Also, consider using <code>~/</code> as a prefix on your paths:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?&gt;
&lt;siteMap xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/AspNet/SiteMap-File-1.0" &gt;
  &lt;siteMapNode url="~/default.aspx" title="Home"&gt;
      &lt;siteMapNode url="~/approver.aspx" title="Approver Expenses" roles="Approvers" /&gt;
      &lt;siteMapNode url="~/audit/auditor.aspx" title="Audit Page" roles="Auditors" /&gt;
      &lt;siteMapNode url="~/admin/admin.aspx" title="Admin Manager" roles="Admins" /&gt;
  &lt;/siteMapNode&gt;
&lt;/siteMap&gt;
</code></pre>
